=============================
📌 EP02 – ADVANCED FOR LOOPS IN DART
=============================

🔷 1️⃣ What is an Advanced For Loop?

These are special or smart ways of using for loops:

✔ Nested for loops
✔ Loop with conditions
✔ Loop with break
✔ Loop with continue
✔ Reverse loops
✔ Looping without initialization or update

These are used for complex logic.

🔷 2️⃣ Nested For Loops (Loop inside loop)

Used when we want to repeat something inside another loop.

✔ Example 1 – Print a square pattern

for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {         // Outer loop controls rows
  print("Row $i");                     // Shows which row we are in

  for (int j = 1; j <= 3; j++) {       // Inner loop controls columns
    print("  Column $j");              // Prints column inside each row
  }
}

📌 Output:
Row 1
  Column 1
  Column 2
  Column 3
Row 2
  Column 1
  Column 2
  Column 3
Row 3
  Column 1
  Column 2
  Column 3

  💡 Why use?

Useful in:

Grids

Tables

Game boards

UI layout loops

🔷 3️⃣ Using break (Stop the loop immediately)

for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
  print("Number: $i");

  if (i == 5) {               // If number becomes 5
    print("Stopping loop.");  
    break;                    // Loop ends here
  }
}

📌 Output:
Number: 1
Number: 2
Number: 3
Number: 4
Number: 5
Stopping loop.

💡 Why use?

Stop searching when item found, stop loops early to improve speed.


.

🔷 4️⃣ Using continue (Skip a step)

for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
  if (i == 3) {               
    continue;                 // Skips printing 3
  }

  print("Value: $i");
}

📌 Output:
Value: 1
Value: 2
Value: 4
Value: 5

💡 Why use?

Skip unwanted records, skip null/invalid data, skip blocked users, etc.


🔷 5️⃣ Loop Without Initialization

Sometimes the variable is declared outside.

int i = 1;                           // Initialized outside

for (; i <= 5; i++) {                // No initialization inside loop
  print(i);
}

📌 Output:
1
2
3
4
5

🔷 6️⃣ Loop Without Update (Manual update inside loop)

for (int i = 1; i <= 5;) {      // No update here
  print(i);
  i++;                           // Update manually inside loop
}

✔ Works same, but gives more control.

🔷 7️⃣ Infinite Loop (Until condition is false)

⚠️ Be careful using this.

for (int i = 1; ; i++) {     // No condition → always true
  print(i);
  if (i == 5) break;         // Stop manually
}


🔷 8️⃣ Real-Life Example 1 – Searching a product

List<String> products = ["Shoes", "Watch", "Phone", "Bag"];

for (int i = 0; i < products.length; i++) {
  if (products[i] == "Phone") {
    print("Phone found at index $i");
    break;                       // Stop searching
  }
}
